{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794545750646,"sessionID":"ses_e2cbe0d40ffeJEGbl89dN2X2ox","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3430f24002OfilL20DYbMHUJ","sessionID":"ses_e2cbe0d40ffeJEGbl89dN2X2ox","messageID":"msg_1d342dce7001tmhyMS4S52QLy9","type":"tool","id":"call_bbadaff35c4f423397e058c8","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"awk '/^- \\[ \\] T007 /{print; exit}' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md | fold -w 190","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"- [ ] T007 [P] Ask the Codex approval check before reading Codex delivery (`OF`, `OT`). Import `fileURLToPath` from `node:url` and define `REPO_ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.me\nta.url)), '../../../../../..')` and `CODEX_CHECK = join(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs')`. Export `codexHookApproval({ projectDir, configPath } = \n{})`: return `'unknown'` when `projectDir` is not a non-empty string, else run `spawnSync('node', [CODEX_CHECK, '--root', projectDir, '--json', ...(configPath ? ['--config', configPath] : []\n)], { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 10_000 })`, parse stdout as JSON and map `code` `codex-hooks-approved` to `'approved'`, `codex-hooks-unapproved` to `'unapproved'`, `codex-advisor-hook-absen\nt` to `'absent'`, `no-codex-hooks` to `'no-hooks'` and anything else, a spawn error or unparsable output to `'unknown'`. In `briefDelivered`, add an option `codexConfig` and a `codex` branch\n before the final return: when `codexHookApproval({ projectDir: locator?.projectDir, configPath: codexConfig })` is `'unapproved'` return `false`. Otherwise return `'unknown'` when `loadSess\nion` is not a function or the load is not ok, `true` when `recordsHaveBrief(loaded.records)` and `'unknown'` otherwise. Add a comment saying an unapproved project hook never runs, so the bri\nef cannot have arrived, while an approved one may store its context where no reader looks yet. In `OT`, add cases on a temporary root holding `.codex/hooks.json` with `{\"hooks\":{\"UserPromptS\nubmit\":[{\"hooks\":[{\"command\":\"node x/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js\"}]}]}}`: an empty config file gives `'unapproved'`, a config holding `[hooks.state.\"<realpath of root>/.codex/hooks.jso\nn:user_prompt_submit:0:0\"]` then `trusted_hash = \"x\"` gives `'approved'`, a root with no `.codex` gives `'no-hooks'`, and `briefDelivered({ runtime: 'codex', locator: { projectDir: root }, c\nodexConfig: <empty config> })` resolves to `false`. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"writeFile|appendFile\" $OF` prints only the existing backfill write.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- [ ] T007 [P] Ask the Codex approval check before reading Codex delivery (`OF`, `OT`). Import `fileURLToPath` from `node:url` and define `REPO_ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.me\nta.url)), '../../../../../..')` and `CODEX_CHECK = join(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs')`. Export `codexHookApproval({ projectDir, configPath } = \n{})`: return `'unknown'` when `projectDir` is not a non-empty string, else run `spawnSync('node', [CODEX_CHECK, '--root', projectDir, '--json', ...(configPath ? ['--config', configPath] : []\n)], { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 10_000 })`, parse stdout as JSON and map `code` `codex-hooks-approved` to `'approved'`, `codex-hooks-unapproved` to `'unapproved'`, `codex-advisor-hook-absen\nt` to `'absent'`, `no-codex-hooks` to `'no-hooks'` and anything else, a spawn error or unparsable output to `'unknown'`. In `briefDelivered`, add an option `codexConfig` and a `codex` branch\n before the final return: when `codexHookApproval({ projectDir: locator?.projectDir, configPath: codexConfig })` is `'unapproved'` return `false`. Otherwise return `'unknown'` when `loadSess\nion` is not a function or the load is not ok, `true` when `recordsHaveBrief(loaded.records)` and `'unknown'` otherwise. Add a comment saying an unapproved project hook never runs, so the bri\nef cannot have arrived, while an approved one may store its context where no reader looks yet. In `OT`, add cases on a temporary root holding `.codex/hooks.json` with `{\"hooks\":{\"UserPromptS\nubmit\":[{\"hooks\":[{\"command\":\"node x/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js\"}]}]}}`: an empty config file gives `'unapproved'`, a config holding `[hooks.state.\"<realpath of root>/.codex/hooks.jso\nn:user_prompt_submit:0:0\"]` then `trusted_hash = \"x\"` gives `'approved'`, a root with no `.codex` gives `'no-hooks'`, and `briefDelivered({ runtime: 'codex', locator: { projectDir: root }, c\nodexConfig: <empty config> })` resolves to `false`. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"writeFile|appendFile\" $OF` prints only the existing backfill write.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"awk '/^- \\\\[ \\\\] T007 /{print; exit}' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md | fold -w 190\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794545749796,"end":1794545750646}}}}
