{"type":"text","timestamp":1794545985522,"sessionID":"ses_e2cbe0d40ffeJEGbl89dN2X2ox","part":{"id":"prt_1d3469ee7001w0GIb40kg5bDoc","sessionID":"ses_e2cbe0d40ffeJEGbl89dN2X2ox","messageID":"msg_1d3468d56001COUQwQCCMKqdQ2","type":"text","text":"T007 is implemented in the two named files. `VO` passes and `TC` exits 0. The third verify clause prints two pre-existing lines, not one, because its regex also matches the existing `writeFileSync` import.\n\nFiles written (only these two):\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`\n\nWhat changed in the module:\n\n- Added the `fileURLToPath` import and `REPO_ROOT` / `CODEX_CHECK` constants.\n- Added exported `codexHookApproval({ projectDir, configPath })` with the four code mappings and `unknown` fallbacks.\n- Added the `codexConfig` option and the `codex` branch in `briefDelivered`, with the comment that an unapproved hook never runs while an approved one may store its context where no reader looks yet.\n- Added four tests: unapproved, approved by trusted hash, no hooks file, and `briefDelivered` returning `false` for an unapproved Codex hook.\n\nVerify output:\n\n1. `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` in `ADV`\n\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  15 passed (15)\n```\n\n`VO_EXIT=0` (baseline was 11 passed, so 11 existing plus 4 new).\n\n2. `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`\n\n```\n> typecheck\n> ../../system-spec-kit/node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit --composite false -p tsconfig.build.json\n```\n\n`TC_EXIT=0`\n\n3. `rg -n \"writeFile|appendFile\" $OF`\n\n```\n26:import { existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n392:  writeFileSync(outPath, output.map((line) => `${JSON.stringify(line)}\\n`).join(''), 'utf8');\n```\n\nThis does not literally print only the backfill write. Line 26 is the pre-existing import, and line 392 is the pre-existing backfill write. No new write path was added. As a second receipt, `git diff -U0 HEAD -- $OF | rg \"^[+-].*(writeFile|appendFile)\"` prints nothing and exits 1, so neither line is part of this change. I did not alter code to satisfy the literal wording.\n\nAlso observed: `node --check` on the module exits 0, and `git status --short` names only the two files above as modified.\n\nNot done, because the task forbade it: the T007 checkbox is untouched and no `[B]` mark was written into `tasks.md`.\n\nOperator action: decide whether the pre-existing import match satisfies the third verify clause or T007 should be marked `[B]` with the output above. Nothing is blocked on me.","time":{"start":1794545983207,"end":1794545985522}}}
